Project context — mock3 (two codelines, both TypeScript + vitest, ESM with "type":"module"):

Codelines and layout:
- mocka at /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-a — source under src/, tests under test/ (e.g. test/fares.test.ts imports from ../src/fares). Ticket MOCK3-1 concerns src/fares.ts: fareFor uses `rider.age > 65` (strict greater-than) but the doc comment on the same function says "Riders aged 65 AND OVER pay the concession fare." A rider aged exactly 65 falls through to BASE_FARE_CENTS instead of CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS. The only caller is totalFor in the same file, which delegates to fareFor — blast radius is contained within src/fares.ts. Existing tests cover ages 30, 8, and 70 but never assert the boundary at exactly 65; that is the test gap the spec must close.
- mockb at /home/bradleyjerome/projects/mock3/mock-b — source under src/, tests under test/ (e.g. test/schedule.test.ts imports from ../src/schedule). Ticket MOCK3-2 concerns src/schedule.ts: formatStops loops `for (let i = 0; i < stops.length - 1; i++)`, which omits the final stop. The sibling totalMinutes correctly reads `stops[stops.length - 1]`, confirming the last stop is expected in rendered output. Existing tests assert the first stop name and the arrow separator but never assert the last stop appears; that is the test gap the spec must close.

Build, type-check, and test commands (identical in both codelines):
- Run tests: `npm test` (executes `vitest run`)
- Type-check: `npm run build` (executes `tsc --noEmit`; tsconfig has strict:true, noEmit:true, target ES2022, moduleResolution "bundler", include ["src","test"])
- Lint: `npm run lint` (no lint configured — echoes a placeholder string)

Conventions:
- Test files live in test/ (not co-located with src), named <module>.test.ts, using vitest describe/it/expect and importing from ../src/<module>.
- TypeScript strict mode is on; any change must type-check cleanly under `tsc --noEmit`.
- Both fixes are one-line logic changes: change `>` to `>=` in mocka's fareFor age check, and change `stops.length - 1` to `stops.length` in mockb's formatStops loop bound. Acceptance criteria should require a test at the exact boundary (age 65 for mocka, last stop in output for mockb) that fails before the fix and passes after.

